ns with the first team, Ramos established himself as an integral player for the club, helping them win the league title in 2022–23. In 2023, Ramos signed for Paris Saint-Germain on an initial one-year loan deal, before joining the club permanently for €65 million.\r\n\r\nRamos is a former Portugal youth international, representing his country at various levels, including the under-19 team that finished as runners-up at the 2019 UEFA European Championship and the under-21 team that finished as runners-up at the 2021 European Championship. He made his senior international debut in 2022, being part of the squad at the 2022 FIFA World Cup.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strGender":"Male","strSide":"","strPosition":"Centre-Forward","strCollege":null,"strFacebook":"","strWebsite":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"www.instagram.com\/goncaloramos88\/","strYoutube":"","strHeight":"1.85 m (6 ft 1 in)","strWeight":"78 kg (172 lb)","intLoved":"0","strThumb":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/player\/thumb\/ki0ein1770217883.jpg","strPoster":null,"strCutout":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/player\/cutout\/47dx051766335509.png","strCartoon":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/player\/cartoon\/6dj0az1770217906.png","strRender":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/player\/render\/k0tkdf1704574289.png","strBanner":null,"strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strCreativeCommons":"Yes","strLocked":"unlocked","strLastName":"Ramos"},{"idPlayer":"34421267","idTeam":"133714","idTeam2":null,"idTeamNational":null,"idAPIfootball":null,"idPlayerManager":null,"idWikidata":null,"idTransferMkt":null,"idESPN":null,"strNationality":"Spain","strPlayer":"Guillem Hernández","strPlayerAlternate":"Guillem Hernández Folguera","strTeam":"Paris SG","strTeam2":"","strSport":"Soccer","intSoccerXMLTeamID":null,"dateBorn":"1994-03-05","dateDied":null,"strNumber":"","dateSigned":null,"strSigning":"","strWage":"","strOutfitter":"","strKit":"","strAgent":"","strBirthLocation":"","strDeathLocation":null,"strEthnicity":"","strStatus":"Coaching","strDescriptionEN":null,"strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strGender":"Male","strSide":"","strPosition":"Assistant Coach","strCollege":null,"strFacebook":"","strWebsite":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"","strYoutube":"","strHeight":"","strWeight":"","intLoved":"0","strThumb":"https:\/\/r2.thesportsdb.com\/images\/media\/player\/thumb\/qopbzj1760892589.jpg","strPoster":null,"strCutout":null,"strCartoon":null,"strRender":null,"strBanner":null,"strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strCreativeCommons":"No","strLocked":"unlocked","strLastName":"Hernández"},{"idPlayer":"34246715","idTeam":"133714","idTeam2":null,"idTeamNational":null,"idAPIfootball":"446249","idPlayerManager":null,"idWikidata":"Q129088593","idTransferMkt":"1185888","idESPN":"388522","strNationality":"France","strPlayer":"Ibrahim Mbaye","strPlayerAlternate":"","strTeam":"Paris SG","strTeam2":"","strSport":"Soccer","intSoccerXMLTeamID":null,"dateBorn":"2008-01-24","dateDied":null,"strNumber":"49","dateSigned":null,"strSigning":"","strWage":"","strOutfitter":"","strKit":"","strAgent":"","strBirthLocation":"Trappes, France","strDeathLocation":null,"strEthnicity":"Black","strStatus":"Active","strDescriptionEN":"Ibrahim Mbaye (born 24 January 2008) is a French-Moroccan and Senegalese professional footballer who plays as a forward for Ligue 1 club Paris Saint-Germain.\r\n\r\nClub career\r\nMbaye started his youth career in 2013 at ES Guyancourt before joining Versailles in 2015. In 2018, at the age of 10, he joined the Paris Saint-Germain Academy. In the 2023–24 season, while aged 16, Mbaye helped the PSG under-19s achieve victory in the Championnat National U19 play-offs, scoring against Marseille in a 2–0 win in the semi-finals and participating in the 3–1 victory over Auxerre in the final.\r\n\r\nOn 14 July 2024, Mbaye was called up for pre-season with Paris Saint-Germain's first team, having impressed head coach Luis Enrique. On 7 August, he made his first appearance and start for the club in a 2–2 friendly draw against Sturm Graz. Nine minutes into the match, he scored PSG's first goal of the season after receiving an assist from Marco Asensio. Following PSG's second pre-season match on 10 August against RB Leipzig, in which Mbaye was a starter, Luis Enrique praised Mbaye's performance, saying he was satisfied with his play. On 16 August, Mbaye made his official debut for PSG, playing the first half of a 4–1 victory away to Le Havre, the first match of the 2024–25 Ligue 1 season. He became the youngest player to start a game for PSG at 16 years, 6 months, and 23 days, surpassing the record of his teammate Warren Zaïre-Emery.\r\n\r\nInternational career\r\nMbaye is a youth international for France. At the 2024 Montaigu Tournament, he helped the France under-16s achieve victory while picking up the award for the competition's best player.\r\n\r\nPersonal life\r\nBorn in France, Mbaye is of Moroccan descent through his mother and Senegalese descent through his father.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"